In this article we relate the set of structure preserving equivalent martingale measures $(\mathcal{M})$ for financial models driven by semimartingales with conditionally independent increments to a set of measurable and integrable functions $(\mathscr{Y})$. More precisely, we prove that $(\mathcal{M}
ot = \emptyset)$ if, and only if, $(\mathscr{Y}
ot = \emptyset)$, and connect the sets $(\mathcal{M})$ and $(\mathscr{Y})$ to the semimartingale characteristics of the driving process. As examples we consider integrated Lévy models with independent stochastic factors and time-changed Lévy models and derive mild conditions for $(\mathcal{M} 
ot = \emptyset)$.

